From ea07395f05ea581e6ebc941c1047c5e2c2391dbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:38:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Test the Path/str boundaries fixed in the pathlib follow-up

Reverting all twelve hunks of "Fix Path/str confusion left over from the
pathlib migration" and running the suite gives a byte-identical result --
`6 failed, 3560 passed, 31 skipped, 44 errors` either way. None of its eight
fixes was exercised by anything, including the two that produce silently
wrong output rather than an exception.

`tests/test_path_str_boundaries.py` covers all eight call sites, asserting
the result rather than the absence of an exception, because for the two
silent ones there is no exception to catch. Reverting each hunk on its own
turns the matching test red:

* `generate_training_dataset/frame_extraction.py`, `extract_frames` --
  `assert [] == [False]`; the `set[Path]` the GUI passes matched no video in
  `video_sets`, the extraction loop never ran, and `all([])` reported
  "Frame extraction failed. Video files must be corrupted." about a video
  the test had just written.
* `refine_training_dataset/outlier_frames.py`,
  `ExtractFramesbasedonPreselection` -- `assert None == (5, 40, 7, 30)`; the
  crop from `video_sets` was dropped, so frames come out uncropped and the
  labels are plotted un-offset.
* `refine_training_dataset/outlier_frames.py`, `find_outliers_in_raw_data`
  -- `AttributeError: 'PosixPath' object has no attribute 'endswith'`.
* `utils/conversioncode.py`, `analyze_videos_converth5_to_csv` --
  `AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'name'`; and
  `analyze_videos_converth5_to_nwb`, checked one call earlier because
  `dlc2nwb` is optional.
* `pose_estimation_tensorflow/modelzoo/api/superanimal_inference.py` --
  `AttributeError: 'PosixPath' object has no attribute 'split'`.
* `utils/plotting.py`, `plot_trajectories` -- `TypeError: sequence item 0:
  expected str instance, PosixPath found`.
* `pose_estimation_tensorflow/predict_videos.py`, `AnalyzeVideo` --
  `cv2.error: ... Can't convert object of type 'PosixPath' to 'str' for
  'filename'`, which is the crash that started the patch.
* `gui/tabs/create_videos.py`, `CreateVideos.create_videos` -- `TypeError:
  sequence item 0: expected str instance, PosixPath found`.

Each site is tested with both a `Path` and a `str`, since two of these fixes
are for the reverse confusion.

The videos are real, written with `cv2` into `tmp_path`, and the project is
a real one from `create_new_project`, so the configs are the real thing.
Where a call site cannot be reached without a trained model or a running
QApplication the surrounding machinery is stubbed and the boundary itself is
left alone: the GUI test calls `CreateVideos.create_videos` unbound on an
object carrying the attributes the method reads, which needs `qtpy` to
import the module but no display and no `QApplication`.
---
 tests/test_path_str_boundaries.py | 452 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 452 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/test_path_str_boundaries.py

diff --git a/tests/test_path_str_boundaries.py b/tests/test_path_str_boundaries.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cd48a99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/test_path_str_boundaries.py
@@ -0,0 +1,452 @@
